  ('zcrm_1579374000148509099', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000020299015', 'Brittany Perrotto', NULL, '10.09.2024 Brittany called back in, feeling sad and hopeless with the high lab bill that was sent to her from her preventive visit. An appointment that she expected to be covered fully, turned out to be almost $700.
Brittany''s appointment was sometime in the summertime (maybe in July), for an annual physical. She was not aware that she needed to call us ahead of time, given she''s been with this membership for over 5 years. Therefore, when she went in for her appt, she proceeded as she had in the past. It is possible that elements may have changed without her knowing. [Maybe we can encourage members to experience a refresher "course" when new services/guidelines/laws surface in their memberships?].
We did a 3-way call with Planstin, and spoke with the wonderful William, who went over the details of the labs to help confirm and educate. He shared that the metabolic panel is not the same as the cholesterol lipid panel - Therefore - not ACA guidelines.
Both William and I ran out of options to see how to diminish or decrease that lab bill for Brittany. We could both hear the quiver in her voice, due to the surprise amount that she now owes. 
She repeatedly shared that should she have know it would not be covered, she would have taken the option for cash pay, which was $60. She requested the physician to reverse the billing, after she received the $700 bill, but he/she said it would be insurance fraud if he did that. 
I told Brittany that I would try to reach out to my MPB admin team to see if there''s anything we can do to help her with this bill. I do not think she has the money, and was on the verge of tears on the phone. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-10-09 15:30:30', '2024-10-09 15:49:30'),
