  ('zcrm_1579374000148242008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000145560002', 'Stephanie Thompson', NULL, '100.07.2024 Stephanie called left a message, asking for Nahla. I called her back and we talked about the medications she''s searching to see if at all covered, or will she just pursue them via coupon:
estradiol minivelle .05
Trazodone hcl 50mg
Pravastatin 20mg
Over the phone, I searched CostPlus Drugs, My Free Pharmacy and called ARM to learn two things; if the stated medications are covered via the preventive lens & if they can proceed in helping Stephanie see the below physicians via the RBP model (according to Catherine''s suggestion last week, on Friday, to connect ARM with the providers ahead of time/prior to the appointment, so they can make the arrangement in billing). 
Providers are not in network: OBGYN - GP/PCP - a 3-way call? YES around 3:30CT.
Dermatology is in network - PHCS Practitioners and Ancillary.
My call to ARM was not fruitful, as the representative shared that she does not have any authority over such actions, and that we most likely need to speak to Lori, who at the time was at lunch. I told Stephanie that I will go ahead and call on her behalf, so I''m not taking anymore of her time. Stephanie then went ahead and emailed me her providers'' information, so I can present them to ARM, when I get someone on the phone. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-10-07 13:06:47', '2024-10-07 15:13:24'),
