  ('zcrm_1579374000148129013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000142862002', 'Victoria Shavlik', NULL, '10.04.2024 Victoria called not knowing what to do with the receipts she has from paying for appointments she had today 10/4. I asked what type of appointments they were, and she said preventive. She had paid for them. So I told her, if they were preventive they should not have been paid for. 
I helped her find her card in her email. Suggested that she call back her provider and get reimbursed from the angle that she is still learning how to use her membership, as it is super new. Then present them her ARM card and the information on the back. Victoria will proceed with those steps, and call us back if she needs additional assistance. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-10-04 17:51:54', '2024-10-04 18:03:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000148129008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000126940021', 'Deborah Aulita', NULL, '10.04.2024 Christina called to get set up on CirrusMD. I sent her the registration link successfully. She will call me back if she has any trouble. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-10-04 17:12:31', '2024-10-04 17:12:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000148129003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000009474065', 'J. Vance Andersen PLC', NULL, '10.04.2024 Vance called with his son Landon, trying to get connected with telehealth. I tried sending Landon an invitation link, but it did not recognize his credentials. The rest of the family was good to go, but not Landon. I sent in a ticket as I was speaking to Vance, and while I was setting that ticket up, Vance was registering himself and the family. I guided Vance to how to connect with a physician from the laptop. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-10-04 16:58:40', '2024-10-04 16:58:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000148034342', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000148499229', 'Justin Wamsley', NULL, '10-4-24 Justin is 42 and he''s marrying Edgar tomorrow who is 29. Justin is Type 1 Diabetic and uses metformin, has high blood pressure and high cholesterol. Takes lamictol and something else.  I let him know of the pre-x and exemptions. Edgar has ADHD and takes Adderall.  I explained everything to Justin and he enrolled for Nov. 1st, Secure HSA ES $1000/$555 in 2024. Justin Walmsley - $555 month in 2024 and $578 in 2025 - Justin''s portion is $325 and Edgar''s is $210 / 2 = $105 as Justin''s portion to pay in 2024, $242 / 2 = $121 for Justin to pay in 2025. THIA pays 100% for employee and 50% for spouse or children. No dental/vision.  He''s considering if he wants life insurance since he''s going to live forever. He and Edgar are foster parents in Longmont! They have 4 kids they are fostering right now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-04 16:55:09', '2024-10-04 16:55:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000148034332', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000148499180', 'Deanna Sais', NULL, '10-4-24 I sent this to Vinnie and the Team also via Tix - The prices on https://joinmpb.com/the-hope-institute-of-america/ enrollment platform look wrong. For 50-64 it should be $405 in 2024 and $419 in 2025. However, as I enroll my new member it''s showing $416.20. I have no idea where that number is coming from. Any idea? Can you fix it. I''m enrolling her now as List Bill, so it should get corrected in the background.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-04 15:59:28', '2024-10-04 15:59:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000148034322', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000148499180', 'Deanna Sais', NULL, '10-4-24 Deanna is turning 50 on 10/10/24 born on 10/10/1974. She has a husband and son who are on her husband''s plan for medical and dental. She doesn''t have any pre-x, but she takes allergy meds for seasonal allergies, no tobacco or smoking. She was hired by The Hope Institute on Sept. 23rd, 2024 as Office Admin in new office in Boulder.  She is familiar with HSA''s and had one from a previous employer but used the funds in the account. She''s open to starting a new account and THIA will fund it $150 per month. She is also interested in a life insurance policy but only the $25 that is being offered. I gave her the items to have ready for our next appt next Friday.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-04 15:58:23', '2024-10-04 15:58:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000148122001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109660008', 'Larry Essex', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 3888 Question : I want to cancel my enrollment. I want it effective today, since I had to leave message again, lime every other time I have tried to contact a human', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2024-10-04 15:31:31', '2024-10-04 15:31:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000148098087', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116236002', 'Lisa D''Onofrio', NULL, '10/4/24: Lisa called. After helping her organize her MPB links, log into her member portal, bookmark tabs, and providing her with credentials and ID#s, Lisa asked if I could see the recent bills she submitted to Zion. 
We called Zion to make sure they have everything on their end and can see the recent submissions. Isabella said it looks like the processor (Chelsea) may have moved some items around within her sharing request, but it is currently being processed. We weren''t able to speak to Chelsea directly. LVM for her to give Lisa a call back to provide update. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-10-04 14:45:21', '2024-10-04 14:45:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000148098077', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109179002', 'Corey Vincent', NULL, '10/4/24: Providers office called to check on a claim status for Christie. I explained that if it were a preventive visit then the claim would be with Planstin, however if Christie''s visit is diagnostic or illness related she is a self pay patient. The woman on the phone had a very thick accent and it was VERY DIFFICULT for us to decipher one another. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-10-04 14:07:54', '2024-10-04 14:07:54'),
