  ('zcrm_1579374000147984008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028471248', 'Charles Christian Figge VI', NULL, '10-3-24 Figge called bc his card for meds no longer worked. He was converted to PSDHC by John Kach in Dec. 2022 it looks like. He believed he had wellness and he clearly showed the RCI card for his medications. They told him it was no longer active anymore. Per Admin123 he has PSDHC and is paying $321 while he''s still 49. He was asking about mental health, dental and vision and wants to do his wellness visit and is open to doing a skin check since it''s been a long time as well. His activities are all outdoors and free such as biking and such. His pre-x are migraines, ADHD and sleep which he takes meds for. Probably best to leave him on his current membership. I gave him the price for increasing IUA to $1500 or dropping MEC and adding HAB.  $1000/$321 is what he has now. $1500/$299 if he increases IUA. Or, he can drop MEC which makes it $255.15+$15 = $270.15 + $107 HAB = $377.15 for SDHC + HAB at $1000 IUA.   If he increases IUA to $1500 then he saves $23 making it $247.15 + $107 = $354.15.  He needs to ponder. The mental health part alone will make it beneficial.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-03 13:51:03', '2024-10-03 13:51:03'),
