- Preventive coverage for colonoscopy where the provider is in network, but the facility is not.
Nicholas does not remember receiving a bill, but wants to make sure they''re using appropriate parties to maintain coverage. 
I shared information that was shared with me by a MEC representative saying, it''s ok if the facility is NOT in network, but as long as the provider is. I also proceeded to say, to pretend that I am wrong on that information, Planstin does have the RBP model to fall back on, and all you have to do is guide the facility to connect with Planstin for billing. 
Nicholas will connect with Planstin to verify the steps to maintaining coverage for preventive, as well as ask about the Planstin Member Portal situation, and will follow up with Zion on the mammogram sharing request.
He also asked about the difference between Secure HSA vs. Premium HSA. I recommended to speak with Misty. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-09-30 17:49:14', '2024-09-30 17:59:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000147681021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116236002', 'Lisa D''Onofrio', NULL, '09.30.2024 Lisa called with a lot of anxiety over numerous bills, accumulated from her husband''s death on 08/2023, her daughter''s illnesses and ER visit on 09/27/2023 = ER visit = ~$10K bill, and other miscellaneous doctor visits, which may or may not be preventive.
Lisa has been dealing with various emotionally heightened situations, since she was enrolled with, and played a lot of phone tag and reciprocation regarding completion of her welcome call, so she NEVER GOT THE EDUCATION on how to use her membership.
She shares how overwhelmed she was at that time, and did not know who to turn to.
She''s been paying out of pocket for all of her bills, and most likely not via the cash pay patient discount. Daughter kept getting sick - had a hard time fighting basic colds. 105 fever rendered her to the ER visit.
- She finally got diagnosed with allergic asthma - never had that her entire life - is on inhalers now and they want her to do allergy shots. THIS is when Lisa started panicking and wondering if she EVEN has AN INSURANGE. Not understanding the nature of her membership with MPB.
I initiated helping her via membership education at first: 3 major parts (Essentials, Preventive & Health sharing) and what each one is responsible for.
I then started addressing one issue topic at a time:
- Daughter''s ER visit = possible sharing request with Zion
- Daughter''s multiple doctor''s visit (allergy & derm) = possible sharing requests with Zion
                       * Derm appt = removal of mole > biopsy > noncancerous
- Her paying for several visits and using the Planstin card for everything = called Planstin to attain any EOB''s and learn any details: Dates, amounts, guidance from here.
- Husband''s death = CANNOT collect from Zion on "Death Assistance...", husband died from Cancer 08/2023. Member has not completed their 1 year membership as of yet.

HW for Lisa: Call the hospital and request the cash pay patient price for the ER visit.
HW for Nahla: Have admin reach out to Lisa with a new advisor to help her through her membership, including possibly changing the membership or at least the IUA, if interested. 
HW for both: Lisa will call back TOMORROW and ask for Nahla to take that 3-way call we attempted tonight with Planstin (they were not available to answer our call, so she will call back tomorrow to try again). NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-09-30 16:09:31', '2024-09-30 16:45:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000147681013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000144155019', 'Trevor Pacheco', NULL, '09.30.2024 Learned via the spreadsheet from Julia that Alexa''s birthday is wrong in the system, and their information is not coming up in CirrusMD. 
In order to proceed with the ticket to CirrusMD, I called to attain the correct birthday information, but I ended up leaving a VM instead.

Alexa called back PROMPTLY, after listening to the message. It turns out, it is Trevor''s birthday that is incorrect. It is showing as July 30th, 1989. The CORRECT BIRTHDAY ( I changed it in the CRM) is June 30th, 1989. I will put in a note to Patti to change in the Admin123. 

Once that is corrected, I will put in a ticket to CirrusMD. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-09-30 15:39:07', '2024-09-30 15:43:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000147681008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116613002', 'Timothy Foley', NULL, '09.30.2024 Meryluz called asking if we are the same as Cigna, and I explained how we are not.
She proceeded to also ask about her preventive options, and I gave her brief details. Then I sent her, via Outlook, details and visuals to help her maneuver her appointments. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-09-30 15:35:37', '2024-09-30 15:35:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000147609036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000103167002', 'Teresa Broaddus', NULL, '9/30/24: Teresa called. She''s having some labs drawn tomorrow and wondering what Planstin will cover. I advised that they will pay for a lipid panel and diabetes screening but not her Thyroid lab. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-09-30 14:46:45', '2024-09-30 14:46:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000147609031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111775010', 'Xiaosong Xiao', NULL, '9/30/24: I spoke to Danielle - the Zion Processor working on Sean''s sharing request and learned the following:
The second request keeps getting deleted by her bc both requests are for the same issue.
Zion will share into the Park Nicolette bill however not for "preventive services" or vaccines.
Member will have to request a patient ledger or superbill from hospital visit in Nicaragua in order for it to be shared by Zion - they cannot collect this information on his behalf. 
Emailing Member these updates and will work on getting Park Nicolette bill submitted to planstin and request he have new cards sent over. 
AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-09-30 14:12:55', '2024-09-30 14:12:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000147609026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000139268002', 'Donna Trocino', NULL, '9/30/24: Donna emailed the following message:
I keep getting emails from Zion Healthshare to sign a PHI authorization form. Is this a part of your company and am I supposed to sign this form?

Response: Hi Donna,
I wanted to clarify that Zion Healthshare is the medical cost-sharing group associated with your plan. Typically, the only time you would need to sign a PHI (Protected Health Information) form is if you wish to authorize someone else to discuss an open Sharing Request with Zion on your behalf.
While it’s not technically required, Zion encourages this practice to ensure that a spouse, older child, or someone close to you can assist with your medical needs if necessary.
I hope this information is helpful!
AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-09-30 14:09:36', '2024-09-30 14:09:36'),
