  ('zcrm_1579374000147454021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000144387001', 'Penny Black', NULL, '9/27/2024
Penny called to ask for information on how to get her COVID and flu shots covered. She was told at Walgreens that she needed to go to the doctor''s office to get it covered. I informed her that she could go to the dr office to get both of them covered instead of getting them in the pharmacy and she told me I was wrong and not to give out the wrong info. I offered to do more research for her regarding the situation and give her a callback. She also wanted to speak to Nahla regarding a voicemail she left (I will relay that info to Nahla )
FYI. 
I called Arm, CVS, and Walgreens will not cover COVID-19 vaccines due to a contracting issue ARM members should go to any other big pharmacy chain instead.', 'Acelyn Calderon', 'Acelyn Calderon', '2024-09-27 09:31:04', '2024-09-27 09:33:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000147519041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000147520081', 'Lisa McCann', NULL, 'Member was going to go on Sedera direct so Sedera made an exception for this member to be effective 10/1/24', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-09-27 09:26:48', '2024-09-27 09:26:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000147452140', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000075974121', 'Maria Crompton', NULL, '9/27/24: Maria called asking where she can go to get urine tested. She''s having issues with a UTI. I advised that if she wants to have a test done she could go to her PCP or an urgent care clinic, OR utilize CirrusMD but Cirrus of course wouldn''t be able to run a urinalysis. She asked if the urgent care would be covered. I explained no, that only preventive services are "covered" but if the issue is illness/injury related then she is self pay until the issue exceeds $1000. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-09-27 09:21:43', '2024-09-27 09:21:43'),
