  ('zcrm_1579374000147238014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081869008', 'Frederick Koen', NULL, '09.24.2024 Tina called regarding an incident (her accent and speed talking made the conversation a little unclear, however I asked clarifying questions to be sure to understand her question) that involves a bone fracture (unsure who), and how to get shared if TODAY''s appointment, would render them over the IUA.
We went over staying organized for sharing requests: presenting as cash pay patients, collecting all receipts, and submitting them and remaining balances and bills onto the sharing request with Zion. Tina did say they already have a portal open with Zion, and the sharing request was asking her for a specific amount, so I explained that is usually for planned procedures and it comes from a good faith estimate. She will learn more today from the doctor on what the future entails for this bone fracture, and how she will proceed to get shared or not.
She also asked if she has any preventive through Zion, I said no, but her advisor Wendy DOES offer preventive services through Health Access Benefits, HAB. She will connect with Wendy for more information. 
It was a pleasure speaking with Tina, but paraphrasing what she asks is important due to the way she talks and sound of her accent. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-09-24 08:29:58', '2024-09-24 08:29:58'),
