  ('zcrm_1579374000146744013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000112215002', 'Brenda Harms', NULL, '9-16-24 Brenda is trying to get her colonoscopy paid for by Planstin but the provider is in-network and the dr. is not. Here''s how she should proceed according to guidance from Planstin.

"Please have Brenda contact her provider and request they send us a claim – or have her call us and we can assist her with her provider.
 
If the provider is out of network and won’t submit a claim, she can send us the claim for reimbursement (because she has RBP). We would need the receipt/bill showing all the CPT and diagnosis codes.
 
Note- she has 6 months from date of service to submit the claim to us for reimbursement."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-18 16:27:27', '2024-09-18 16:27:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146744008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031391042', 'Jonathan VanNoy', NULL, '9-18-24 Jon called to find out pricing for Benjamin on his own or with his soon to be spouse. They are getting married on Oct. 18th or so. I recommended Premium Care since they are young. He will be 26 in Oct. and she''s about 22. At the $1500 IUA it''s $212 EO or $456 ES. They will decide and let me know hopefully by tomorrow.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-18 16:23:32', '2024-09-18 16:23:32'),
