  ('zcrm_1579374000146624038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000145836002', 'Brian Gurinsky', NULL, 'Left a detailed message on vm. Sent email to book online the welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2024-09-17 11:13:21', '2024-09-17 11:13:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146647026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027674051', 'Michelle Searles', NULL, '9-17-24 CSU refused everything we sent even though none of their stipulations make sense. Shelly is open to one of the grandfathered healthshares or trying C4. If we do C4, perhaps we get the lowest cost possible option and she can keep her current membership.  She wants to keep her on her current membership. So, this is what I proposed...

"You bring up a good idea. You will not save any money by cancelling Georgia and you are not required to cancel her membership. We could look at the absolute cheapest Connect for Health CO option to appease CSU and keep her on your current membership.  Your current membership would then be considered secondary to the new insurance plan. We can''t look at the plans for 2025 yet since they won''t be released until Nov. 1st. I''d day this is the best path at this point. Perhaps reach out to me in early Nov. and we''ll take a look."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-17 11:05:31', '2024-09-17 11:05:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146625019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064414873', 'Jillian Livingston', NULL, '09.17.2024 Jillian called with a couple of questions:
1- Husband eventually needs knee replacement, BUT NOW will be getting steroid shots - would Zion share?
