  ('zcrm_1579374000146647003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064414873', 'Jillian Livingston', NULL, '9-17-24 Jillian called to confirm what she was told for her husband''s knee. She was told by Acelyn not to submit the steroid injections for her husband''s knee if he then wants a knee replacement down the road. Steroid injections I don''t believe are alternative. So, this doesn''t sound quite right. I think it''s standard procedure to try the injections first and if they don''t work then they move to surgery. She will call back later and speak with Nahla to be certain. She also wanted to inquire about her colonoscopy one more time. She will check to make sure everything is in-network and bill it through Planstin. If any portion is deemed out of network, she will run that through HAB. If it turns diagnostic, she knows that she will have to pay her chosen IUA and run it through Zion. Colonoscopies are capped at $5 ONLY if it turns diagnostic. From the Sharing Guidelines, "Injections related to an eligible sharing request are shareable up to $5,000."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-17 09:01:52', '2024-09-17 09:01:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146642003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064414873', 'Jillian Livingston', NULL, 'called regarding colonoscopy coverage, I advised to confirm with the medical facility if they are in phcs network, i also explained when it  would turn diagnostic and not preventative. i also explained the RBP policy plansin has how ever the dr does have to agree to it(incase the facility is not in network)
