  ('zcrm_1579374000146440072', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032016379', 'Maurine Killough', NULL, '9-11-24 Maurine had trouble with HMA today. Hollie wasn''t nice to her or her provider and wasn''t willing to look into where the FAX they sent went or something along those lines. She said Geoff Kirk would call them back. Maurine paid for her visit. The dentist will still try to submit the claim for reimbursement/payment and they will pay Maurine back if it''s successful. I sent Maurine these instructions to share with her provider.

Direct line for provider questions: 281 - 436 - 9674
To process claims please instruct provider to upload bill here:
https://www.healthmatching.com/provider-portal
 
INSTRUCTIONS:
Page one: Insert NPI ID (provider identification number) in one of the four provided boxes on page one, depending on provider type.
Page two: Insert provider information such as: Provider''s name, phone number, service facility location, billing address, W9, and tax ID number.
Page three: Upload Bill
Confirmation and receive claim number to track the claim 

FOR COPAY REIMBURSEMENTS
PLEASE LOGIN AT www.healthmatching.com
AND REFER TO THE ORANGE TAB THAT READS
COPAY REIMBURSEMENT AND ADD NEW.
COPAYS ARE ONLY UP TO $50


Coming September 15, 2024 we will be having new program updates that will include:
Reimbursements: Reimbursements for bills you paid out of pocket for. However, those will only be honoring service dates of September 15, 2024 and forward.

You can submit these on www.healthmatching.com by logging in and selecting payment reimbursement on the orange bar on the top of the home page once you login. After selecting payment reimbursement, please select "add new" and submit the itemized receipt and banking information to be reimbursed.


ADDITIONAL INFORMATION:
OUR ADDRESS: 5120 woodway dr. suite 10025, houston texas, 77056
FAX NUMBER: (713) 850-8579 
Thank you,
 
Customer Care
Health Matching Account Services, Inc.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-11 17:11:33', '2024-09-11 17:11:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146440052', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012675060', 'Quentin Green', NULL, '9-11-24 Quentin looks to have original start date  from above at "7-23-20 Choosing MPB CareZ with MEC at $344/$1000."  He''s possibly needing a hip replacement. He''s on OPD and wants to move to CARE+ $350 and HAB $107 which is $457, no disruption to Zion.  His hip is only an issue in the past 8 months. Dr. said it was arthritis and he got an injection. Now, they are saying he might need a full hip replacement. He will inquire about the cash price tomorrow in case there''s any change Zion deems it pre-x. If so, it would be capped at $125K worst case scenario. But, again he''s been a member for over 4 years already. He will call me tomorrow when he has some answers. I also told him to call MPB Concierge to help him determine highest quality care at the fair price locally for this surgery.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-11 16:46:12', '2024-09-11 16:46:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146440044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012675060', 'Quentin Green', NULL, '9-11-24 Looks like CARE+ and HAB is  the best solution to keep the price exactly the same as Accent 360 proposed by Primary Partners. He loses unlimted access to Dr. Varesh Patel in person but he gains additional wellness, dental, vision, gym, etc. $350+$107= $457, plus all MPB benefits. He also said he Never uses Dr. Varesh Patel. So, no need to try to keep him in the mix. He can still see Dr. Varesh Patel for anything he chooses.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-11 16:13:19', '2024-09-11 16:47:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146446039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105086010', 'Ben Rego', NULL, '09.11.2024 I called Planstin regarding the situation above with Ben seeking to have his Annual Physical at an Urgent Care with 100% coverage. I spoke with Celeste and she explained, if they can code it differently than Urgent Care, cz they cannot change it once it reaches them. She also offered to let him know that Planstin is always willing to advocate for the members while they are at the office or do a 3-way call.

I called Ben, it rang successfully, then the ring tone ended, I did not hear anyone on the other end, THEN it gave me a hang up tone. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-09-11 16:10:36', '2024-09-11 16:10:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146440036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012675060', 'Quentin Green', NULL, '9-11-24 Per Patti, "After looking into the OPD structure, the Zion product it''s paired with is the Worksite DPC membership.  So they would have to cancel the OPD membership, then re-enroll in either the Care + or Direct.  Just give me a heads up so I can go in on the back end and "fix" the CRM.  Also they would be subject to the 2024 pricing since Zion would look at this a a "new enrollment".   2025 pricing is just a couple of months away."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-11 16:05:36', '2024-09-11 16:05:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146440031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108048002', 'Joshua Stein', NULL, '9-11-24 Joshua Stein and his wife Emily joined MPB Secure Care as of Dec. 1st 2022. I was just made aware from Josh that they had double memberships. Emily''s employer Thrival Mode joined Zion as a group. His wife Emily joined the employer group in March of 2024. Then Josh joined as the spouse as of June 1st, 2024 while also paying for their Secure Care membership the entire time. 

It sounds like Emily gained her new employment with Thrival Mode in Jan. of 2024 and got her new benefits starting March 1st. Josh thinks Thrival Mode already had Zion signed up as a group prior to Emily''s employment, but he''s not certain. So, at any rate they had double memberships for both of them and for slightly different amounts of time. They are now wondering if they can get some reimbursement from Zion for the overlapping double memberships?  I know MPB can''t reimburse for our portion since that''s all paid out already. But, Zion should never have members paying for two memberships. Clearly they don''t have any way to flag this.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-11 15:56:14', '2024-09-11 15:56:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146440026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001881022', 'Carolyn Tabak', NULL, '9-11-24 Carolyn has decided to stick with Cobra for now until she can review open enrollment. Then she''ll decide if Cobra is best in 2025 or a C4 plan. MCS won''t serve her well with her new pre-x at this point with migraines and sleep apnea. She gets some very expensive injections for her migraines. Her sleep apnea machine is broken onw and she might want surgery to correct her problem. So, I told her we can revisit it all when open enrollment begins.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-11 15:33:49', '2024-09-11 15:33:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146461023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000146087021', 'Jane Kim', NULL, 'called because she wanted to change her IUA to 1000 and change her payment method.
i also explained what therapeutic services are sharable with zion (i just read the guidelines) she''s looking for a chiro.', 'Acelyn Calderon', 'Acelyn Calderon', '2024-09-11 15:17:50', '2024-09-11 15:17:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146442013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109186002', 'Zachary Larson', 'SalesIQ Chat Zachary Reached Out Info 9/11/24', 'Zachary sent a message on our Website via SalesIQ requesting help. He needs to change from paying with a CC to bank withdrawal from now on. I responded via his email address by sending him our Payment Uodate cognito form. Lastly, I informed Patti of his name and situation so she can keep an eye out for his submission. Acelyn mentioned she tried calling Zachary with no answer. All set for now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2024-09-11 14:37:13', '2024-09-11 14:37:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146461018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000135734002', 'Michael Meyers', NULL, '1. wife called to ask what her mec covers because she has some labs getting done
