  ('zcrm_1579374000146270006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108658008', 'Wendy Weiner', NULL, '09.09.2024 Wendy had a colonoscopy on March 6th, the Monarch Anesthesia facility billed her asking for a $1050 for the anesthesia. It sounds like the facility did not bill Planstin, and the time they filed it to Wendy is  way past the 90 day rule at this point.
We decided to do a 3-way call with Planstin, we spoke with Caitlyn. She broke down what she can see in their system:
$5785 is the reprice for the colonoscopy
$493 also paid - preventive

She then guided Wendy on the following:
-    Planstin requests proof of a timely filing to Planstin, and they would honor it, if they facility had not filed in a timely manner. then Planstin will deny it and Wendy will have paperwork. She should not be responsible for it. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-09-09 15:58:15', '2024-09-09 16:11:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146321003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000125284001', 'Marianne Ricciardi', NULL, 'member called because she does not have planstin card she is trying to book an appoitment a.c', 'Acelyn Calderon', 'Acelyn Calderon', '2024-09-09 15:12:21', '2024-09-09 15:12:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146288013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021624001', 'Rachel Holden', NULL, '9-9-24 Rachel called bc Zion has yet again denied her husband of sharing due to some markers that were off from a past dr. visit. Now, he has been diagnosed with prostate cancer. She''s super bummed that they left Zion for 1 year and now they are facing the pre-x clause due to that break. They never thought this random marker would lead to cancer or be an indication of cancer. She will look at regular ins. for Jan. 1st in the Healthcare.gov since they live in MT. She knows the open enrollment begins Nov. 1st and will wait to review those plans for 2025. She will stay on their membership with the rest of the family and just move her husband. The cancer is very slow growing but the cost of the surgery will be around $100K-$140K it sounded like.  It''s not prudent to wait.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-09 14:47:16', '2024-09-09 14:47:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146288008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050504120', 'William Madsen', NULL, '9-9-24 Bill is trying to select Cobra for 3 months and then will choose MPB, Premium Care likely. He was having trouble selecting Cobra. His company will pay the 1st 3 months of Cobra for $1200+. He will sort that out and call me when he''s ready. He will likely join for Dec. 1st now he thinks.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-09 14:28:13', '2024-09-09 14:28:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000146288003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012675060', 'Quentin Green', NULL, '9-9-24 Quentin needs a hip replacement. He''s an OPD member and it''s ending soon.  I''m thinking of DIRECT or the new Secure Elite or CARE+ and HAB. He will hold tight. We have until Sept. 19th at the very least, possibly Oct. 19th. UPDATE - Secure Elite won''t be available soon enough.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-09 13:36:05', '2024-09-11 16:09:52'),
