  ('zcrm_1579374000145803008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000145822001', 'Angelika Hellmer', NULL, '9-3-24 Angelika is 62 and turning 63 before the end of the year. Referred by Krista Rogers. She''s very healthy, only does preventive visits, no meds, takes supplements. She does have a knee issue at the moment and understands that will be 100% her responsibility to pay for in year 1 and then tiered sharing after that. She will join solo, since she was widowed in 2013 and her daughters are 35 and 32. She''s a resident in NM and FL. She has primary in FL and can join Premium Care. She''s tired of our very broken health insurance system and was paying $1100 month to BC/BS for $6500 ded and PPO plan. Then she moved to a Short-Term Medical for 6 months at $640 mo with $1000 Ded. She hates these plans and is tired of paying so much for terrible coverage. She did a colonoscopy at age 50 and did a stool test recently that was undetermined. She needs to do a colonoscopy soon. I explained how it works with Premium Care and separately with HAB. She will find out if they will code it as diagnostic or preventive to determine the best path forward. I also let her know of the 6 month wait with Premium Care but no wait with HAB as long as preventive. She does wellness, dental, vision, gym, etc. She''s happy to include HAB. Chose Premium Care  for $285 and HAB $107 for = $392 month.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-09-03 12:14:04', '2024-09-03 12:14:04'),
