  ('zcrm_1579374000145286003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121310002', 'Cooper Aiken', NULL, '8/26/24: Katelyn called, she cannot find a pediatrician on the PHCS network that is anywhere close to her, but remembered me explaining that she can go out of network. I further explained how Planstin pays for out of network services and to have provider call them if she has any issues setting up appt. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-08-26 07:13:48', '2024-08-26 07:13:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000145255046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011899568', 'Stephanie Yost', NULL, 'appt 7/1/2024 Stephanie went in for a colonoscopy in her area. Except, there''s only ONE facility there that performs that procedure. They had a consult with her, and told her she had to have one, and charged for the consult ~$283.
We did a 3-way call with Planstin, and spoke with Caitlyn. I explained that the members there do not have many choices, in fact (according to Stephanie), that''s the ONLY facility that performs a colonoscopy. In hopes that they can make an exception for members in that area to get covered for the mandated consult.
Caitlyn put us on hold to speak to the higher powers to be. She came back with, looking into getting Stephanie into a newer plan, PA versus PL (RBP), to have the possible option to get reimbursed and such. She then learned that the provider/facility to send the bill to Planstin, or send it again. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-08-23 16:29:26', '2024-08-23 16:38:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000145255041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065104128', 'Lindsay Tollefson', NULL, '08.23.2024 Lindsay needed clarification on how to present and bill/get covered for her preventing annual physical. She ended up paying $35 co pay, after feeling pressured at the providers office to present her card. They read what on there and followed along, instead of listening to her present herself. I recommended she request that they reverse that, to no co pay. 
In addition, they tested for labwork that was not under the ACA guidelines, and that created a total amount of ~$85 out of pocket, when it should have been zero. We spoke with planstin to make sure of the accuracy, and it turns out they tested for 3 non preventive ACA covered labs. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-08-23 15:36:53', '2024-08-23 15:36:53'),
