  ('zcrm_1579374000144721026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000127235001', 'Pamela March', NULL, '08.15.2024 Anthony went to the hospital 7.14-15.2024. Zion dropped their benefits on 6/30th. They adhered to the 30 day window, submitted the sharing request, got denied.
Still showing active for Pamela, but for Anthony was dropped end of June, not sure why.
Amber from Zion transferred us to Planstin to fix the date drop.
Karen from Planstin shared that they end the membership the month before they age into 65. She double checked on this fact with and it turns out it is Zion''s guideline they follow, but no one brought that fact to surface:
1- Not when it was about to take place (prior to 6/30).....
       a- They were traveling but they made sure their mail was forwarded.
2- Not via phone call (prior to 6/30)
3- They called to open a sharing request - and were told he does not have benefits anymore. That''s how they learned of it.
4- They invited them to use the 30 day window, and they did
5- Zion denied the sharing request due to the  date membership ending on 6/30
6- They want to appeal...... the 3-way phone call with Zion and Planstin (one sitting) was like a ping pong match.
7- There''s absent communication in this situation and no accountability to clear up mistakes
8- The guidelines don''t show support of ending benefits 30 days prior to the member aging out month.
I reached out to Julia before I went out to lunch. She said she will read the guidelines and we will reconvene. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-08-15 13:34:17', '2024-08-15 15:54:15'),
