  ('zcrm_1579374000144192118', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106694002', 'Renee Hornor', NULL, '08.07.2024 Renee called concerned about a surgical procedure that was billed to Planstin by the provider, vs Renee getting the opportunity to get it shared, via already open and approved sharing request, by Zion.
Some of the charges are ~: $3000 for the Dr.s fee and $1500 for other services, were misbilled to Plansti, by the provider.
Renee tried to talking to them to change the coding, b/c naturally Planstin rejected it, and b/c they did that the provider coded it "COSMETIC". WITH THAT CODING, Renee''s procedure will not be shared.
The provider shared they cannot change the coding as that would be insurance fraud, and that Planstin rejected it b/c it is not covered. Neither of that is accurate according to previous member/provider interactions on billing mishaps, and according to Neri from Planstin and her billing requirements education.
I proposed we speak to Planstin and learn what exactly was submitted and communicated to know what leverage or cards to play with the provider.
Neri (Nedi) from Planstin with Renee - 3 way call.

Some BILL FACTS:
1- Sent anesthesia to Planstin, and doctor bill went to Zion
2- When Planstin is billed, THEY have to process it.

According to their system there was no reciprocation of language on the billing. Just processing the bill from them.
T', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-08-07 13:04:31', '2024-08-07 13:04:31'),
