  ('zcrm_1579374000144226148', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175892262', 'Michelle Zlakowski', NULL, '8-7-24 Michelle just turned 50 and her son is 12. She owns her own business. She has been on her significant other''s employer plan but they just broke up. Her plan will probably go until end of Aug. or Sept. She''s not sure. She lives in or near Arlington, VA. No pre-x other than inquiring about 1 polyp that was removed in a routine colonoscopy. I''m asking Sedera how they deem that. Also, son takes anxiety meds. She watched the video and I told her the differences of the pre-x clause and payment to member first for the Premium Care. She can get a subsidy through ACA and can pay only about $400+ for the two of them bc of her income level. So, that may work better for her for now. I also quoted HAB but that brings the cost too high for her. Premium Care alone is best. Son is on anxiety meds and she''s hoping to get him off of them soon. She wants to be able to get his childhood immunizations included at no cost. I''m awaiting the response from Sedera. Premium Care $1500/$533 for 30-64 and HAB would be $200 more which seems like a stretch for her right now. $2500/$463 might be in alignment with her budget.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-08-07 12:05:14', '2024-08-07 13:33:29'),
