  ('zcrm_1579374000144074072', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120264002', 'Cheryl Powell', NULL, 'Cheryl sent me an email askign what the IUA is. I replied with the following:

Good Evening Cheryl,

Your current IUA level is $1000. (Good choice ?)

The Individual Unshareable Amount (IUA) is simply the personal financial responsibility of the member. Once a medical need occurs, the member pays their IUA, and once the IUA is met, the health sharing community steps in and assists in medical bills. Members and Households that experience multiple Needs Cases within their 12-month Membership Year are required to pay the first three IUAs at the selected amount. If there is a fourth Needs Case during the same Membership Year, no IUA would apply. This is great because it limits your financial exposure to a maximum of 3 x''s your chosen IUA level.

For example, if you had a bad year with multiple medical events and you are at the $1,000 IUA level, the maximum out of pocket cost would be $3,000 (3 x $1000).

I hope this helps and I''d be happy to get on a call with you to answer further questions. 

Best,

Kirk', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2024-08-01 17:32:09', '2024-08-01 17:32:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000144115061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000096329001', 'Christopher Cappuccitti', NULL, '8-1-24 Chris called me back immediately. They are going without any benefits for now while they start their own biz. They can get a subsidy through Penny(?). But he mentioned he submitted his W2 and not his 1099. I let him know he will need to reveal 1099 as well to avoid penalties down the road. He was grateful. He''s open to new options in the next months or turn of year. He sees the cancellation form in his inbox and will complete it right away.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-08-01 15:48:31', '2024-08-01 15:48:31'),
