  ('zcrm_1579374000144024114', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000138128002', 'Justin Caid', '07.31.2024 SENT MPB''s Permission to Discuss MPB Membership with Megan', '07.31.2024 Justin''s wife, Megan, called to learn how to submit bills as a cash pay patient. I realized she was not on the membership, so I sent Justin the MPB Permission to Discuss the details with Megan.
She brought Justin on the line, so then we can speak freely, till he completes the form.
I explained the process of the cash pay patient, collecting the receipts, adhering to the IUA and the 6 month deadline. I even mentioned the app, where they can upload all of their receipts and documents in one place. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-31 17:22:17', '2024-07-31 17:22:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000143961048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081634027', 'Julia Bolz', NULL, '7-31-24 Dear Julia Bolz,

Congratulations on purchasing a Direct Vision plan!

Please take the time to review your order details as well as our terms of service. If you have any questions, call us at 844-833-8440 or e-mail us at info@directbenefits.com.

Do not respond to this confirmation email. Allow 5-7 business days for your application to be processed. Your cards and plan information will be delivered electronically or mailed in 7 to 10 working days to the address you provided in the Primary Enrollment Information section.  

Plan includes a one-time non-refundable enrollment fee of $25. This charge will be made at the time of purchase and may appear as a separate transaction from your insurance as Direct Vision or Direct Benefits, Inc.

Your specific coverage information is as follows:

Plan Selected: VSP Choice Plan A
Who’s covered: Applicant
Effective Date: 08-01-2024
Carrier: Ameritas
Monthly Charge: $15.97

Policy Number: 300119417
Agent Info: Wendy Scipione (Phone : (720) 259-1555) 

Direct Vision | www.directvisioninsurance.com
844-833-8440', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-31 16:50:10', '2024-07-31 16:50:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000143961043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058024128', 'Marjorie Wolter', NULL, '7-31-24 Marjorie Wolter submitted her cancellation form just now. She called me to cancel and I wasn''t able to help her in time bc my power has been off and on for two of the last 3 days. Even my cell service wasn''t working at times. So, I was able to reach her finally and she completed the form immediately. She already has chosen Impact Health for Aug. 1st start date. She doesn''t want to deal with self-pay. Apparently Impact Health gives her an insurance card to use instead.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-31 16:48:40', '2024-07-31 16:48:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000144024101', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123199001', 'Carey Reynolds', NULL, '07.31.2024 Carey sent us an email yesterday concerning a preventive mammogram that she has been trying to schedule for a while now. 
According to Carey, from what I am understanding, the facility she''s trying to go to is not willing to bill Planstin.
Her email included her advisor, Wendy Scipione, who responded to her with extra information from the member experience lens with that same facility. She suggested that she reach out to her, so she can get to the bottom of it and guide Carey to her next steps, since other members with Wendy DO USE that facility for imaging with no problem in billing Planstin.
I called Planstin and spoke with Caden, sharing the above scenario, and he kindly said that they will reimburse the member, and proceeded to list all that would be required in the email to, claims@planstin.com, to get reimbursed. I shared this information with Carey and Wendy via response to Carey''s email. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-31 16:37:56', '2024-07-31 16:42:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000143961038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064414873', 'Jillian Livingston', NULL, '7-31-24 Jillian chose to keep Planstin since the savings is negligible. She included Patti in her email early this morning. I''ll make sure Patti saw it.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-31 15:49:15', '2024-07-31 15:49:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000144024090', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000019362044', 'Therese Antonino', NULL, '07.31.2024 Nirri from Planstin called confirming the type of membership Therese and Mark have. I double checked on Admin123 and the only discrepancy that showed to me, was whether it is a M+S or M+Child. Patti, via teams chat, confirmed it is M+S. Then I transferred Nerri to her for further clarification. 
******************************************************************
Later on, Mark calls the concierge sharing that a member of their family spoke with Jane Kassel, and she shared with them that she has not signed up anyone for the last two years in Washington under MPB, cz they would not be covered.
******************************************************************
I did offer a bit of possibilities that they may have been grand-fathered in, prior to the law taking place on healthsharing in Washington, which is why they were able to use Planstin coverage on their cologuard and annual physical.
Then I strongly suggested they have a serious conversation with Jane Kassel, given she is their advisor for further guidance and options, to be prepared and not be left without coverage/benefits. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-31 15:29:44', '2024-07-31 15:44:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000144003123', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031391042', 'Jonathan VanNoy', NULL, '7/31/24: Member called to find a primary care doctor. I guided her on how to search the multiplan network, and emailed her my results page. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-07-31 15:08:31', '2024-07-31 15:08:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000144003118', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000004658165', 'David Abookire', NULL, '7/31/24: Elsa called asking how to access 30% fullscript discount.
I led her to site and link, but when she clicked on it - it took her to her current fullscript account which doesn''t have 30% off. I emailed the link which she said did the same thing. Suggested she log out and create a new log in. She asked if there is a discount code - asking and will let her know tomorrow. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-07-31 14:43:43', '2024-07-31 14:43:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000144003110', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124216002', 'Bradon Erickson', NULL, '7/31/24: Carmen from Planstin called - she had a provider on the phone and they were wanting to know if member had any additional prescription benefits through MPB. I explained that no - just what they can get through planstin, reimbursements for approved medication under an open sharing request, and we can search for discounts and coupons for members. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-07-31 14:03:26', '2024-07-31 14:13:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000144047381', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000144055012', 'Kate Wasserman', NULL, 'Member Only $5000 IUA Secure w/RCI', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-07-31 13:34:46', '2024-07-31 13:34:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000144024082', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028257276', 'Jacqueline Martinez', NULL, '07.31.2024 Jacqui called to get an extensive education on her membership to relay to her financial advisor, who was concerned about them being slighted by being on a healthsharing company vs a traditional insurance.
Usually, I would refer the members to schedule or schedule another welcome call with Vanessa, where she can spend a vast amount of time going through EACH service provided through MPB.
HOWEVER, this was to convince/educate the financial advisor that not all healthsharing companies are like Liberty, and although there are a lot of moving pieces, the members are always empowered, have options, guidance, advocacy and more.
We also went into details on how Sedera specifically treats their members when it comes to medical needs. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-31 13:34:01', '2024-07-31 13:37:04'),
