  ('zcrm_1579374000143747039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109380001', 'Louis Nappi', NULL, '07.25.2024 Dawn called and left us a VM regarding an email she received 3 days ago.
I called her back today, and she clarified what she was worried about, needing to re-enroll each year, is actually not what the email was about, but it was to inform the members to look out for the upcoming charges from MPB. 
She also had questions about her daughter who turned 25 in May, 2024, and wanted to confirm that she indeed can stay on her plan, even though she is now married.
I messaged Kirk via Teams chat. I did get a response from Kirk, so I told Dawn I would email their advisor and Cc them on it, as I did and BCc''d Reba, the advisor trainer. I gave Dawn Mike Montes'' phone number to call him if they need to. 
EMAIL:
"Greetings Mike,

I hope your Thursday has been good to you.

I had the honor to speak with one of your loyal members, Louis and Dawn Nappi. I was able to answer some of Dawn''s questions, and I will include them here in case anything has changed without my knowledge, as well as the ones I do not feel confident to fulfill an answer to for them. In hopes, that you could shed light in a detailed & effective fashion.

The Nappi''s inquiries are:
How long can a dependent child stay with the family membership?  I shared that they may stay, up to the age of 26th.
If a child dependent gets married, can they stay on the family membership, since they do not have benefits anywhere else? 
If the answer to question #2 is a yes, the other part to that question is: Can there be sharing benefits for maternity endeavors? I shared, if the answer to #2 is a YES, then Zion does have an impeccable package in their guidelines to share the costs for maternity specific needs.

Thanks again Mike. The Nappi family is looking to hear back from you before the weekend, to better prepare for their daughter, and have ease of mind.

Thank you for all that you do.

Nahla Tebcherany
MPB Health
Concierge Consultant
800-519-2969

* Disclaimer *

This email is intended solely to provide supplementary information to our valued members and is not a personal point of contact.

If you have additional questions or concerns, please call the Concierge at 1-800-519-2969."', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-25 16:30:55', '2024-07-25 16:47:11'),
