  ('zcrm_1579374000143255133', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000143308002', 'Hannah Neumeyer', NULL, '7-18-24 Hannah originally was thinking of keeping her ACA Healthcare.gov plan bc she was paying $185 and gets 4 generic meds for $3 each. But, now her employer is offering her healthcare and is paying towards it. Her cost will be $200 and the company will pay the rest. She may lose her subsidy if she keeps  her ACA plan. She will be better off bc she can get her mental health counseling and her check up psychiatrist visits reimbursed up to $3K with HAB. She was paying a discounted rate of $120 for those visits 3-4x a year. She takes these meds: 
lemotrigine 200 mg
buspirone 10 mg 
buproprion SR 100 mg
methylphenidate HCL 20 mg
They appear to be around $3-$15 per month via GoodRX/Pharmacy Checker, etc. and for 3 months.  She chose CARE+ at the $1000 IUA/$265 and HAB $107. It will be List Billed. All set for Aug. 1st with CARE+. Still need to complete HAB enrollment.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-18 21:34:22', '2024-07-18 21:34:22'),
