  ('zcrm_1579374000142866039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000144228001', 'Cynthia Franceus', NULL, '7-11-24 Cynthia 2/5/65 and her husband, William Bjornholm 1-31-66 have Cobra that is ending 7/31/24. She is managing cancer since 2021 and needs to keep her doctors. They moved here from NY 1 1/2 years ago. I sent her instructions to join C4 and add me as agent. We are meeting next week to discuss options. I asked her to send me her list of drs. as well to research in advance.  They don''t have any income right now and have no idea what they will have down the road. She doesn''t want Medicaid. So, I will just have to give her the full price and they can figure it out later if they could qualify for a subsidy.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-11 22:29:00', '2024-07-11 22:29:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142866031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123199001', 'Carey Reynolds', NULL, '7-11-24 Carey and Craig want to move to traditional ins. They are willing to wait for open enrollment. I shared with them America''s Choice as an option but also showed them all of the limitations and concerns I have. They want everything to be easier. They were told they couldn''t get their wellness visit done at BCH but I coached her on just giving them her card. Pretty much everyone who accepts ins in Boulder County accept the PHCS network. She didn''t really know she could be coached by the MPB Concierge Team for wellness either. She wants her meds to be easier to get bc the coupons often don''t work and then she''s running around bc the pharmacy doesn''t know how to process them correctly. She really likes Express Scripts. I don''t know which, if any of the current insurance options through C4 use Express Scripts but it''s a moot point right now. They don''t have a SEP.  I also shared HAB and they are strongly considering that since it has so many more benefits and no network to worry about. If they drop Planstin MEC it''s $90 and add HAB it''s $165. They pay $650 now. It would be $560 + $165 = $725. She will let me know what they decide by the 18th. Also, Craig gets a heart check that they had to pay for and wanted a co-pay. He just has high cholesterol and they use the heart check to prescribe him statins. They are interested in getting a skin check as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-11 21:35:32', '2024-07-11 21:37:18'),
