  ('zcrm_1579374000142627008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000141544019', 'Nicholas Williams', NULL, 'No response. Left a detailed message on vm. Sent email to reschedule welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2024-07-09 07:43:44', '2024-07-09 07:43:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142555416', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120998002', 'William Chilton', NULL, '07.08.2024 William called in to learn if it is NOW a good time to  open a sharing request towards the second year tier of a preX condition. I told him, yes, since they have passed their 1st year waiting period tier from 7/1/2023 to 7/1/2024.
William already has attempted a sharing request in the past with Zion, and has a mbr portal open with them already. I guided him to go through that portal to open the sharing request and give them 3-5 days to respond back with a processor. 
We talked about the 6 month deadline, and that they have that amount of time from this wednesday, when she has her chemo appointment. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-08 17:02:34', '2024-07-08 17:12:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142576036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017830168', 'Laura Zaunbrecher', NULL, '7-8-24 Laura called to obtain her 1095 form for 2023. I will refer her to the Concierge and/or to the Planstin platform.  Left her a vm just now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-08 17:02:04', '2024-07-08 17:04:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142576028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064414873', 'Jillian Livingston', NULL, '7-8-24 Jillian is interested in HAB and 1Dental. They will use the wellness screenings, dental cleanings, vision screenings, gym memberships for sure! The mental health she is trying to use MAP with M&S. They also want to use a psychiatrist to prescribe meds. But, she''s now moving towards brain mapping therapy to reduce or remove meds altogether life long. They will make up the cost of HAB simply by using the dental, vision and gym reimbursements for all 4 family members. She will talk with her accountant about funding the HSA for 2024 and what''s allowed. She needs a colonoscopy every 3 years bc they found polyps the first time 3 years ago. With Planstin, she will likely have to pay her IUA first bc it''s less than the 10 year or 5 year stipulation with ACA and HAB. I''m inquiring with HAB if they will reimburse for this as a new member. For dental, her husband needs gum implants. He''s planning to see Dr. Karina Redko with Snowmass Village Dental for his normal Dental work. For the gum implants, he''s looking into Grand Junction Periodontics. I couldn''t find anyone in the networks. I sent Jillian the link to search on her own. She wants to join and just to find dentists who are in the networks to get the 15%-60% discounts since they have a lot of dental needs. Also, one kid is in NY and the other in another state. So, it will probably work well for them.  They are considering dropping Planstin to save $110 per month. They do fund their HSA and will talk with their tax professional to decide if it makes sense to keep or not.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-08 16:50:55', '2024-07-08 17:42:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142555411', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110363002', 'Zane Pitzer', NULL, '07.08.2024 Zane called to learn how to enroll their upcoming newborn. We went over the Zion''s guidelines for adding newborns through an already approved sharing request, and who to do that with. We did a 3-way call with Zion, spoke with Mandy who clarified that all they need to remember is to make sure to add the baby within the 30 days of birth time. Zane will call Christine Corsini to attain the premium per month after adding the baby. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-08 16:03:42', '2024-07-08 16:03:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142576023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000142598002', 'Heather Bingaman', NULL, '7-8-24 Heather is 41, 4-17-83, daughters are 12, 12-12-11 and 10, 9-26-13. Riley just broke her wrist on May 21, 2024 and Heather didn''t have any health ins bc she left Elevations in fall of 2023.  She worked for them for about 20 years, even when Elevations used to be called Heritage Bank or Credit Union. They are closing or already closed the office in Louisville. She was a branch manager for a long time. She didn''t choose Cobra bc it was so expensive. She has a new job now and the owner will pay 50% towards the cost of her membership. Her other daughter''s name is Kennedy. They are all healthy, no pre-x other than Riley''s wrist, no meds, no tobacco. Yes, they go to the YMCA in Lafayette, they get a ski pass and do other activities for the gym membership. Yes, to wellness, dental, vision, maybe nutrition, no mental health, yes, labs and immunizations, no skin check. She is paying for her membership and is a W2 employee. So, CARE+ $1000/$450 is the best option at her age and as W2. She was thrilled to learn about HAB as well, $200 EC. She enrolled immediately for an Aug. 1st start date. She works at the Louisville Street Faire selling drink tickets at the north or south side with her 2 daughters. She will be there this Friday. I''ll look for her if I go!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-08 15:19:25', '2024-07-08 15:19:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142555385', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000133307002', 'Felix Costa', NULL, '07.08.2024 Rosemarie called wanting to learn how to be covered to go see an Endocrinologist. Mainly a preventive appointment. We talked how that would be considered a nonpreventive appt. To learn that she''s seeking a woman wellness visit, and wants to learn more about the preventive services as part of her membership. 
We went over: the ACA guidelines under Planstin, how to find a physician, how to present at a prev appt, prescriptions, discounted labsites.....etc. 
They do have their planstin card, and so I did explain the RBP vs. the PHCS network approach. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-08 15:06:57', '2024-07-08 15:39:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142576018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025756253', 'Robin Beck', NULL, '7-8-24 Hello Robin,

Your Health Access Benefit is made up of three key pieces that work together to provide you and your family with quality health care. These are your primary care, prescription, and preventive care.

Below you''ll find your personalized Digital Membership Packet, which includes all the information you need to get started using your Health Access Benefit.


Health Access Member ID: 522190696

Benefits Start Date: 07/01/2024

Primary Care
Status: Not enrolled.
When to Use: Your membership does not include any Direct Primary Care services.


Prescription
Status: Enrolled automatically!
When to Use: Use your prescription service anytime you need to fill a prescription from a pharmacy.


Preventive Care
Status: Enrolled automatically!
When to Use: Use your preventive care service to get reimbursed for preventive medical services anytime you visit a lab or doctor’s office for dozens of tests and services.


You''re Done! How Easy Was That?
There is no further action you need to take to activate these benefits. If you are ready to use your Health Access Benefit, instructions are included in your digital membership packet here.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-08 14:06:55', '2024-07-08 14:06:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142595003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091048002', 'Jessica Couch', NULL, '07.0824:  Jessica texted me a group text along with her friend Charlene. She said Charlene currently has Medi-Cal and recently broke her foot. She needs to look for a new insurance plan as her foot heals and asked if I can speak with her about Jessica''s plan. I responded yes and asked Charlene when would be a convenient time for a call to discuss her needs. Her phone # is:  916-342-2556.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2024-07-08 13:32:56', '2024-07-08 13:32:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142592014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111923312', 'Matthew Joppich', NULL, '7/8/24: Matt called. He''s never used preventive services before. His child is having a physical done and wanted advice on how to use plan for service. I advised to use planstin card and present that to provider for billing. We checked the his provider under Multiplan - it didn''t pull up as being in network.
I advised to call provider, and let them know you have a plan that pays 100% of preventive services listed on healthcare.gov and make sure they are willing to bill planstin directly. If they aren''t, then call us back and we can assist in helping find a provider that is in PHCS network. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-07-08 13:32:56', '2024-07-08 13:32:56'),
