  ('zcrm_1579374000142592003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000046294019', 'Melany Matheson', NULL, '7/8/24: Melany called. Her husband had a routine preventive Colonoscopy done 2/13/24. It was clear, no polyps found. They are having trouble with RCI paying for the procedure. RCI has paid for the anesthesia, but not the colonoscopy. RCI is claiming it is not coded correctly and to please have facility re-submit the claim with correct coding. 
Melany stated the claim has been re-submitted now 4 times, with the procedural code 45378 with modifier 33. According to the provider and Melany this means...
"45378 is the base code for a diagnostic colonoscopy. Modifier 33 means "preventative service", and is added to the base code when the procedure is a screening exam".

Melany says that RCI will not provide her with the correct code, instead just keeps asking her to have provider re-code as preventive and re-submit. 
* The facility is stating this is the code used for all preventive colonoscopies.

I let Melany know I would present this situation to my supervisor, and see if we can discuss the claim with RCI and find a solution - and will update her via email of steps taken to resolve the issue. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-07-08 13:14:14', '2024-07-08 13:18:42'),
