  ('zcrm_1579374000142237153', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120745001', 'Louis Marchetti', NULL, '07.01.2024 Louis called and left us a VM saying that they are taking their son to the ER, and need guidance as to how to proceed. I called him back, but the VM picked up, I did leave a detailed VM saying to present as a cash pay patient and even request the cash pay discount. I left our number too so they call us back conveniently. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-01 17:58:09', '2024-07-01 17:58:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142237136', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000020299094', 'Donald Thessen', NULL, '07.01.2024 Misty Berryman put in a ticket to learn if Donald has any MEC in his plan. I first looked him up here in the CRM and he shows that he is still SELF DIRECTED, but when I search for him in Admin123, he shows up as changed plans to SEDERA SELECT+.
I shared the above findings in response to the email/ticket - Misty Berryman. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-01 16:19:18', '2024-07-01 16:19:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142237122', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089149002', 'Daniel Connelly', NULL, '07.01.2024 Cynthia called to solve a balance bill of $102.~
She understands she does get a Gyno under the ACA guidelines, and wants to know why she is getting a bill/did the provider submit the bill to Planstin.
Caitlyn said she does see 3 things:
$605 on 7/10 Preventive visit $431.35 - CODE 99213 for that Gyno visit + specialist. 
After Caitlyn''s explanation of benefits that she was viewing we understood that the provider coded a portion of the bill under "specialist" and that did not get covered by Planstin.

Cynthia now needs to call her provider to clarify the coding of the ENTIRE appointment as preventive under the ACA guidelines, so Planstin can cover it 100%. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-01 15:07:32', '2024-07-01 15:12:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142287021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003158023', 'Lorene Cecilia', NULL, '7-1-24 Lorene''s husband is getting ins through his employer and can add her at no extra cost. So, she wants to cancel for the earliest possible date which is Aug. 1st.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-01 15:04:27', '2024-07-01 15:04:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142229056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000034221050', 'Lily Williams', NULL, '7/1/24: Lily called asking about her HMA account. I informed her that MPB doesn''t manage HMA accounts. She realized she had called the wrong number and hung up. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-07-01 15:03:41', '2024-07-01 15:03:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142229051', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011659413', 'Brad Uhlig', NULL, '7/1/24: Denise called asking how to get her son registered for CirrusMD. I registered him while we were on the phone and asked her to have Marcus look for an email from Cirrus MD with a link to set up his username and password. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-07-01 14:28:57', '2024-07-01 14:28:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142229046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032454006', 'Georgannna Garrison', NULL, '7/1/24: Georganna called requesting to speak to Nahla since she had already been working with her regarding her issue. Relaying message to Nahla to give member a call back. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-07-01 14:06:33', '2024-07-01 14:06:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142229041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128566001', 'Chad Bockius', NULL, '7/1/24: Jamie called asking how to start a need. She is trying to schedule surgery. I gave her steps to open member portal, made sure she was aware of the pre-ex cond phase in period for Zion, and advised to collect an estimate from hospital to submit to hopefully get some of the funds pre-surg. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-07-01 14:01:57', '2024-07-01 14:01:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142287013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000050504120', 'William Madsen', NULL, '7-1-24 Bill realized that his son will need to show proof of ins. Apparently they accepted CARE+ before. I sent him the information about Premium Care to see if they will accept that now. If so, they''ll join for Aug. 1st EC $1000/$533. Otherwise, they could join separately into CARE+ and Premium Care. He would save $8 a month but then have two sets of 3 IUA''s to meet. So, it''s still best to keep them together if the school accepts Premium Care.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-01 13:43:33', '2024-07-01 13:45:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142287008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000143664002', 'Mary Ellen Francescani', NULL, '7-1-24 She needs benefits beginning Sept. 1st. We will enroll EF into CARE+ $875 and ES into HAB $165. They live in PA. She''s taking a leap of faith as she says. She''s been protected with great group ins their entire lives.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-07-01 13:41:10', '2024-07-01 13:41:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142229036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000074947065', 'Andrew Evans', NULL, '7/1/24: Andrew called needing reminding on how to open a need with Zion. I guided him to Zion''s website to his member portal. He was able to successfully get in and begin the process. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-07-01 13:09:23', '2024-07-01 13:09:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142237117', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021919047', 'Tatiana Moroz', NULL, '07.01.2024 Tatiana reached out via site form, straight from Poland asking an international sharing request Zion question. I emailed her via CRM and attached Zion''s website link that hold the guidelines, for her to peruse liberally.
********************************************
Tatiana reached back out wanting more details on how to proceed and inquiries. I sent her the following (1st I sent her info about Zion, forgetting she''s Sedera, so I had to resend the following):
"Tatiana, I AM SO SORRY! Such a long day. Please forgive me.
Your healthsharing company is Sedera NOT Zion. So no, there isn''t a new name for your healthsharing company. Did not mean to confuse you.

Sedera Contact Information in order to open a need:
memberservices@sedera.com
855-973-3372
We usuallyy have the members speak to Sedera to request the link needed to open a portal with them (I don''t know how long it has been since you opened a need with Sedera, so this part might be new to you), so the member can proceed from there to open a medical need.

Same important  details to remember, when requesting for bills to be shared with Sedera:
Open the sharing request, within 6 months of the initial visit.
Fulfill the IUA so Sedera can consider the sharing request.
Be sure to submit all the bills and receipts in a timely fashion, within 6 months of service.
It still needs to be determined shareable or non-shareable with Sedera, depending on the guidelines or pre-existing conditions...etc

As for your initial unshareable amount (IUA) = $500.

I promise you it is not usually this messy. I apologize again, and I''m glad you reached back out before connecting with Zion. I''d love to answer any more questions or guide if you need me to.  
Nahla "                                                                                     NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-01 12:48:28', '2024-07-01 15:54:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142255261', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000132121002', 'Sierra Anderson', NULL, '7-1-24 Called LM for Sierra to fix the billing issue.', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2024-07-01 12:37:06', '2024-07-01 12:37:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142237107', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032454006', 'Georgannna Garrison', NULL, '07.01.2024 Spoke with someone at Zion, received an email from the determination team, regarding her shoulder rotator cuff. Considered menopause as a pre-existing conditions, on accident...will pay for the hormones for a year.
Customer service recommended she reach out to Saunders, Seth (higher up in Zion)... Cami wants to share her thoughts on how Zion is treating women in general, and how they are not caring about saving money from the sharing
RX request for patch
Stem Cells sharing request - pre-x - = will only share up to $125K - but Cami does not want to do surgery - she wants to do stem cell - uploaded all forms possible to be requested onto the sharing request, late February/early March, then it disappeared from the portal - but she JUST checked as we were speaking and they did show up. 
They were still looking for items from the orthopedic medical records, but everything is uploaded.
Did a 3-way with Zion, spoke with Ulysees, I gave a brief intro as to why we were calling, then Cami proceeded in being more detailed in prefacing EVERYTHING from the timeline.
After her explanation, Ulysees went over what he is able to see on his end, and explained that if all the documents were submitted, then it appears that they just need more time to process it all (talking about how it usually takes 5 weeks). He recommended that she connect with the processor, transferred her to leave a VM.
Cami''s concerns are:
1-The reciprocation of the medical need and the progress.
2-Why it was ignored to begin with back in February.
3-Healthsharing/Zion''s treatment of women''s wellness overall.                                   NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-01 12:24:11', '2024-07-01 16:47:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142237102', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000118826002', 'Cathy Baker', NULL, '07.01.2024 Cathy called back, with sharing requests questions and follow up, I transferred her to Zion with coaching. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-01 12:21:16', '2024-07-01 12:21:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142237097', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000030706105', 'Joseph Freije', NULL, '07.01.2024 Joseph called to learn more details on how to connect Zion with the providers regarding the sharing requests he opened. I.E.: He has the PT option that will cost 13K and does not want to pay that upfront. So I told him it is possible to have it paid differently, he just needs to communicate that with Zion and be sure to upload all documents onto the sharing request in time, 6 months. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-01 12:12:45', '2024-07-01 12:12:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142237089', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000132391010', 'Robert Skubiak', NULL, '07.01.2024 Robert called to learn how to proceed with a colonoscopy referred by his doctor and be covered. I walked him through the CoPay plan''s copay for specialists and out of network ordeals. I emailed him via CRM the summary of benefits as well as a snippet of what he might want to view. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-01 12:01:35', '2024-07-01 12:01:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142237076', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000073159147', 'Steven Thomas', NULL, '07.01.2024r Steven called to see if sleep apnea is shared. Unfortunately, even till today, the Zion guidelines DO NOT share that they SHARE anything with sleep apnea. He was of course disappointed. I offered to do some research and call him back if I find anything. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-07-01 11:40:07', '2024-07-01 12:03:11'),
