  ('zcrm_1579374000142065043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106317002', 'Kathryn Reishus', NULL, '6/27/24: All the providers kathy called from our conversation earlier were either not taking new patients or said they wouldn''t take Planstin. Iguided her in trying some different search terms like general practice and internal medicine and giving those options a try and gave Kathy some advice for speaking to providers and urged her to have them call planstin to check eligibility if she has future issues.', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-06-27 15:31:54', '2024-06-27 15:31:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142065038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130364002', 'Doug Eichenlaub', NULL, '6/27/24: Called Doug in reference to missed chat question above. I provided him his member portal information, but what he wanted to do was find a facility for his wife to have a mamm. I guided him in searching the PHCS network which gave a couple results for him to try. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-06-27 15:12:51', '2024-06-27 15:12:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142034091', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000137202002', 'Kristianne Goff', NULL, '06.27.2024 Kristianne called to learn how to proceed with an appointment, she thought it would be preventive, so we discussed that process. Later I learned it actually is going to have to be a cash pay visit, b/c it is a getting a patient established visit. Planstin does not pay for that.
I walked her through to present as a cash pay patient, I sent her links for discounted lab sites and I sent her PHCS lists that she can refer to, when the facility says they do not know who Planstin is or PHCS. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-06-27 15:05:21', '2024-06-27 15:10:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142056028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521119', 'Kallie Carpenter', NULL, '6-27-24 Kallie called back and wanted to make sure they''re still on the best membership. In reviewing it all, they still have the best, grandfathered price. It will be going up $200 from $596.50 to $796.50, but that''s still lower than moving them to anything new. They have had a few needs with Quinn for broken bones. So, they have used it successfully and it''s also better not to start over with pre-x. They also got lucky since the price didn''t increase when Don turned 50 1 1/2 yrs ago. So, she decided to leave it all as is.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-06-27 14:52:21', '2024-06-27 14:52:21'),
