  ('zcrm_1579374000142065028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128527002', 'James Regli', NULL, '6/27/24: Natalie called asking if she has access to Mental Health resources. I explained that she gets 12 sessions her year and provided her with phone number to MAP. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-06-27 13:53:00', '2024-06-27 13:53:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142034073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000141795002', 'Stephen Hillmer', NULL, 'Member &amp; Sp $1000 IUA Premium HSA', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-06-27 13:46:08', '2024-06-27 13:46:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142056018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000145346174', 'Scott Garcia', NULL, '6-27-24 Susan is 57 and husband is 55. They are both self-employed. Susan is best friends with Christine Harvey. No pre-x, no tobacco, yes for wellness. Meds - daughter takes birth control, Susan takes compounded progesterone and estradiol as well as thyroid meds. Husband takes mood enhancer. Both kids are in their 20''s and going to college, sounds like at CU. One has two more years and the other is just starting. They will need to show proof of ins, so I explained Premium HSA to have the MEC as proof of ins for CU. They live in Basalt, CO. I explained that the network is a challenge in Basalt and they can add HAB for the adults, if they want. It''s not necessary for the kids bc they will be well served in Boulder with the MEC. For wellness they do mammo, pap, dental, vision only for husband, gym/ski pass, skin check and no for nutrition. They have Delta Dental through Fire Dept. but it''s looking like it won''t cover wisdom teeth removal for their child.  I will also send them the dental discount plan to review. They don''t really fund an HSA or haven''t in many years. I let her know they could also add $1000 to the contribution to be $8300+$1000= $9300 pre-tax if they choose.  She wants to review it all with her husband. She knows of Sedera through an association or chamber. I forget what she said. I let her know she won''t find what I''m offering directly with Sedera. Also, they need the MEC for compliance with college.  They are paying around $800+ right now but then they wind up paying a bunch of money back when they file their taxes. Husband is a financial advisor.  I discussed Premium HSA EF $1000/$949 or $1500/$860. I suggested they can add HAB for the two adults only at $165 additionally. I forgot to mention the $125/$25. It will be in my email to them next.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-06-27 13:42:55', '2024-06-27 13:42:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142069001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130364002', 'Doug Eichenlaub', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 3677 Question : how do I get registered for the portal ? member id: 1221644353', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2024-06-27 13:34:12', '2024-06-27 13:34:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142065023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106317002', 'Kathryn Reishus', NULL, '6/27/24: Kathy called to find a pcp in an area she will be spending a lot of time in. I navigated her to multiplan and we searched PHCS. There were a lot of results to choose from. I advised to call a few from the list and make sure they are within the network, and if she runs into issues to please give us a call back. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-06-27 13:22:31', '2024-06-27 13:22:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142065013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031044058', 'Samantha Midler', NULL, '6/27/24: Samantha called asking how much a CTA scan is and an Aneurysm Repair Surgery for the brain would be. According to HCBB, CTA scans range from $500-2K and an Aneurysm repair surg. is in the $50K range. I asked Sam if the facility that ordered the scan gave her a price for how much it would be. They did not, so I informed her that she could use HCBB as a negotiation tool if necessary if she is quoted an outlandish price. Emailed her instructions on how to use HCBB to perform her own searches in the future. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-06-27 13:17:42', '2024-10-31 07:13:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142065008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120995010', 'Tom Trimmer', NULL, '6/27/24: Tom called, having issues with finding a provider in PHCS network for a colonoscopy. I advised that Planstin will pay out of network as long as the bill is coded preventive and billed by the provider, and to have the provider call planstin if they have any questions about how to send the claim.
We also discussed IUA, 3 IUA within a 12 month rolling period, and the fact that there are no network restrictions for any illness or injury related service. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-06-27 12:19:26', '2024-06-27 12:19:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142065003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000048401026', 'Angel Ayala Jimenez', NULL, '6/27/24: Aubrey called needing access to log in info to submit a need. On top of that, she stated she never received her fulfillment package or has attempted to access any of her services. I provided her with her MPB Member Portal Credentials, attempted to register her for CirrrusMD with no luck - so sent support ticket to Cirrus via email and instructed member if she didn''t receive an email from them by the end of day, to please give us a call back. Lastly I advised her on how to begin a sharing request, and transferred her to Zion to open her member portal. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-06-27 12:16:30', '2024-06-27 12:16:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142056008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521119', 'Kallie Carpenter', NULL, '6-27-24 Kallie called bc she was just notified of the price change for turning 50 in July. She wants to review her options. I left her a vm.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-06-27 12:14:40', '2024-06-27 12:14:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000142034049', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000139351002', 'Debra Rankin', NULL, '06.27.2024 Debra called and left us a VM. I called her back LVM to call us back.
