  ('zcrm_1579374000141870026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165427', 'April Porterfield', NULL, '6/25/24: april called. The imaging center she is wanting to get her Dexa scan at isn''t listed in network and she wanted to know if she could use the hospital where she got her mamm and bloodwork done since the first few providers listed on PHCS were incorrect numbers. I advised she can go out of network, as long as the provider will bill planstin directly. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-06-25 10:41:17', '2024-06-25 10:41:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000141885016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089965012', 'Michele Palumbo', NULL, '06.25.2024 Michele called right after speaking to Planstin. She seemed distraught and at the verge of crying. She was transferred over there by Angee, and chose #4 to speak to customer service. She initially was trying to connect with Planstin to learn of any progress on the Std Lipid Panel coverage portion from the labs she had done. However, instead of learning of any progress, she was met with a full stop legality fact regarding the 90 day rule. Most members are not aware of that rule, and Michele was caught off guard by the representative''s (she doesn''t know who she spoke with) tone and approach to her situation and inquiry. 
I am unsure of the details of her conversation, other than Michele felt the calm dismissiveness from the representative did not offer her education nor options. She compared her experience with Planstin, with her experience with MPB, numerous times. She looped the conversation many times as well, and I kept bringing her back to the silver lining, being that all of this mishap is to her favor, given the 90 Day rule at hand. 
We had a 50 minute phone call that encompassed her initial problem: a $2098 lab bill, covering the std lipid panel and attaining a discounted price at the discounted lab sites instead to post present to Quest. It also involved her experience with Planstin yesterday, and where to go from here.
I messaged Julia via Teams, and chatted about the 90 Day rule, and the planstin phone call. Julia reached out to the connection at Jason Health ( a discounted website for labs), and Cc''d me on the email, which I responded with extra details to. I relayed the extra information to Michele, as she was still on the phone. 
Michele''s situation is not new. Providers and Labs at seldom times, do not bill in a timely manner. Thus leaving the member scrambling to figure out the bill, when the "insurance" has thrown in the towel right after 90 days.
Michele calmed down after speaking with her, and learned that some team mates at Planstin just have a rough around the edges demeanor, but it does not allow for a dismissal of any subject. Education and patience is key with these situations, and it appears that Julia is in the process of reaching out to Planstin to discuss how MPB members are being treated at Planstin, when they call with heightened situations. 
For the record, Michele DID share the planstin card with doctor when she had her services. It is possible she shared it in May with Quest. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-06-25 10:36:09', '2024-06-26 11:35:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000141870021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108629002', 'Alexander Richardson', NULL, '6/25/24: Kelly called requesting a 1095 form. I advised since she is on the CarePlus plan, there is not insurance component to her plan and that she doesn''t live in an aca mandated state so she will not be penalized for anything related to insurance. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-06-25 10:30:48', '2024-06-25 10:30:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000141885011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000127114002', 'Tracy Campbell', NULL, '06.25.2024 Tracy called to confirm everyone in her family was removed from the membership plan. However, as of today, 06.25.2024, everyone was still there. I checked both platforms, CRM, Admin123 and Cognito to see if she submitted the form. It was submitted on the 23rd of April.
I answered her prev questions, her card questions and she found it in her email. I transferred her to Patti. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-06-25 10:25:13', '2024-06-25 10:25:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000141870016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089965012', 'Michele Palumbo', NULL, '6/25/24: Michelle called. She is very very very uneducated about her plan and how it works. She was essentially calling about the $2K lab bill in the previous note and a urinalysis bill from her well woman exam. She made it seem like she had submitted these labs as a sharing request, and claims that she spoke to Nahla about making sure quest had her insurance info. I explained that must have been planstin as we cannot see into the status of claims nor do we coordinate with providers directly. 
I advised that Michele speak to planstin about the bills and if they were in fact sent to them. Otherwise for the large lab bill, I suggested calling the lab back and asking if she can receive a cash pay discount. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-06-25 10:20:06', '2024-06-25 10:20:06'),
