  ('zcrm_1579374000141260073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084642013', 'Nicole Pietramale', 'New Membership eff 7/1/24', 'Member &amp; Sp $1000 IUA Care +', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-06-18 11:45:49', '2024-06-18 11:45:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000141260068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084642013', 'Nicole Pietramale', NULL, 'Member was sent to me by Karen for pricing to change her IUA from $2500 to $1000 eff 7/1/24.  I gave her pricing and directed her how to fill form out.  She also was unaware of the $60 day wait for IUA to change.  I will process. UPDATE: After looking at the pricing I gave the member the wrong price since her husband just turned 50 price would be $100 more at $520.  I left VM for member to let me know if she wants to move forward.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-06-18 11:44:17', '2024-06-18 11:57:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000141297003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124216002', 'Bradon Erickson', NULL, '6-18-24 Brady somehow got passed off to Kirk which neither of us know why. Brady is looking to add his wife and newborn (4 months) baby to the membership. He''s paying $725 for both of them. He needs to keep SECURE HSA bc he wants to continue to fund the HSA AND he can get a dramatically discounted rate on Skyrizi medication that is $20K without commercial insurance.  Now that he understands the MEC will suffice for this, he''s happy to keep his membership and add his family. He''s looking towards adding them for Aug. 1st after his baby gets more of the immunizations that are already scheduled under his wife''s insurance. With the SECURE HSA w/ RCI at $1000 IUA it''s $763.40 or $2500 / $658.40. This will save them a ton of money since he''s paying $245 for him and $725 for wife and baby which is $970.  So, any option he chooses will be more affordable.   We have an appt scheduled for July 16th to add them.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-06-18 11:35:37', '2024-06-18 11:35:37'),
