  ('zcrm_1579374000140066032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077566026', 'MaiLan Boris', NULL, '05.30.2024 I received confirmation from Planstin that indeed the 1st colonoscopy is NOT COVERED 100% no matter what. The process is like any other time, where it is preventive screening, UNTIL they find polyps to remove, then it is diagnostic. I called MaiLan to share the confirmation, but ended up leaving a voice message to call us back. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-30 16:01:41', '2024-05-30 16:01:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000140066024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000095157002', 'David Stout', NULL, '05.30.2024 Called David to inform him that Planstin has processed his coverage with his provider, and to reconnect with his provider to get reimbursed. I read the note shared on Teams chat by Julia from Ashley Williams at Planstin. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-30 15:51:51', '2024-05-30 15:55:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000140066016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011740129', 'Julia (Wieck) Hardy', NULL, '05.30.2024 Collaborated with Angee about resolving Julia''s bill regarding her Mamm she had in Sept. 
Details:
1- Provider billed Planstin - Planstin paid
2- Member receives another bill from provider for aprox. $60
3- Member does not know what it is for. Planstin will not discuss details of billing with MPB concierge

Instructions for Julia:
1- Call Planstin and request the EOB to view the breakdown of all that was paid, AND a zero balance
2- Call the provider and request clarification for what the $60~ bill is for, when they already billed Planstin and they fulfilled the billing process.

The ball is in Julia''s court to call both parties on Monday she said, and let us know if there''s anything else we could help her with. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-30 15:48:18', '2024-05-30 15:48:18'),
